rationale": "Every major race rater places KS-03 at Safe or Solid Democratic, Davids has raised about $3.7 million to Jenkins' roughly $19,000, and markets give her near-certain odds, so the forecast stays at a comfortable double-digit Democratic margin despite no district polling.", "watch": "Any late independent polling showing Jenkins within single digits or a sudden wave of outside spending against Davids would be the main signals that this call could soften.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Sharice Davids (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Sharice Davids, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in Kansas' 3rd District against Republican Eric Jenkins, with Libertarian Steven Hohe also on the ballot. The district leans modestly Democratic, and no independent general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals and outside assessments. Every major race rater calls the seat safe or solid for Democrats.\n\nDavids holds an enormous financial advantage, raising about $3.7 million to Jenkins' roughly $19,000, and enters the fall with $1.7 million on hand. She won her primary easily and has highlighted bipartisan work on healthcare costs, rural hospitals, and medical supply chains. Prediction markets price her chances near 95 percent. Jenkins has run a low-funded campaign with no reported outside support. The combined evidence points to a comfortable re-election, with the main uncertainty coming from the absence of district polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9826, "margin": 15.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9781, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.979, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9714, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 14.5}, {"date":